    "reading-passage": {
      "nodeId": "542:1649",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "📖 Reading Passage",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "📖 Reading Passage"
        },
        {
          "text": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Living Room",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Living Room"
        },
        {
          "text": "A Room for Everyone\n\nThe living room is the heart of our home. It is where the whole family comes together in the evening to relax, chat, and spend time with each other.\n\nIn the centre of the room, there is a large sofa and two armchairs arranged around a coffee table. My father usually sits in the rocking chair by the window and reads the newspaper. My younger brother prefers the ottoman — he uses it as a seat while he plays on the game console connected to the television.\n\nWe have a tall bookshelf against the wall, filled with books, photo frames, and a small plant in a vase. Next to it is the TV stand with a sound bar and the Wi-Fi router tucked behind it. All the cables go into a power strip hidden behind the cabinet.\n\nThe room feels warm because of the details. There is a soft rug on the floor, cushions on the sofa, and a throw blanket draped over the armchair. My mother hung curtains that match the colour of the walls, and she placed a few candles in candle holders on the side table.\n\nFor lighting, we have a ceiling light for bright evenings and a floor lamp in the corner for softer light when we watch TV. String lights decorate the shelf during holidays.\n\nOn weekends, we sometimes play board games or put together a puzzle on the dining table. Other times, we just sit down, listen to music through the speaker, and take a nap. The living room is not the biggest room, but it is definitely the most loved.",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "A Room for Everyone The living room is the heart of our home. It is where the whole family comes together in the evening to relax, chat, and spend time with each other. In the centre of the room, there is a large sofa and two armchairs arranged around a coffee table. My father usually sits in the rocking chair by the window and reads the newspaper. My younger brother prefers the ottoman — he uses it as a seat while he plays on the game console connected to the television. We have a tall bookshelf against the wall, filled with books, photo frames, and a small plant in a vase. Next to it is the TV stand with a sound bar and the Wi-Fi router tucked behind it. All the cables go into a power strip hidden behind the cabinet. The room feels warm because of the details. There is a soft rug on the floor, cushions on the sofa, and a throw blanket draped over the armchair. My mother hung curtains that match the colour of the walls, and she placed a few candles in candle holders on the side table. For lighting, we have a ceiling light for bright evenings and a floor lamp in the corner for softer light when we watch TV. String lights decorate the shelf during holidays. On weekends, we sometimes play board games or put together a puzzle on the dining table. Other times, we just sit down, listen to music through the speaker, and take a nap. The living room is not the biggest room, but it is definitely the most loved."
        },
        {
          "text": "Comprehension Questions",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Comprehension Questions"
        },
        {
          "text": "1. Where does the father usually sit in the living room?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "1. Where does the father usually sit in the living room?"
        },
        {
          "text": "2. What does the younger brother use the ottoman for?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "2. What does the younger brother use the ottoman for?"
        },
        {
          "text": "3. What items are on the bookshelf?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "3. What items are on the bookshelf?"
        },
        {
          "text": "4. How does the family make the room feel warm and cosy?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "4. How does the family make the room feel warm and cosy?"
        },
        {
          "text": "5. What activities does the family do in the living room on weekends?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "5. What activities does the family do in the living room on weekends?"
        }
